##
FizzBuzz.

The classic first exercise, and a fair look at Profi-C's control flow: a range loop that
reads as a sentence, an if/else-if chain with no parentheses around the conditions, and a
function that yields a string.
##

global model Program

    function Main()
        for n = 1 to 20
            Console.WriteLine(Program.Describe(n));
        end for
    end function

    ##
    Divisibility by 15 has to be tested first. Testing it last would never be reached,
    because 15 is divisible by 3 and the chain stops at the first branch that matches.
    ##
    string function Describe(integer n)
        if n % 15 == 0
            yield "FizzBuzz";
        else if n % 3 == 0
            yield "Fizz";
        else if n % 5 == 0
            yield "Buzz";
        end if

        yield n.ToString();
    end function

end model
